# ABP Authorization

## Permission Definition
Define permissions in a `PermissionDefinitionProvider` class in `*.Application.Contracts` project:

```csharp
public class MyPermissionDefinitionProvider : PermissionDefinitionProvider
{
    public override void Define(IPermissionDefinitionContext context)
    {
        var myGroup = context.AddGroup("MyModule");
        var permission = myGroup.AddPermission("MyModule.MyEntity.Create");
        permission.AddChild("MyModule.MyEntity.Edit");
    }
}
```

## Permission Naming Convention
- Use format: `ModuleName.EntityName.Action`
- Define as constants: `MyModulePermissions.MyEntity.Create`
- Localize using `LocalizableString.Create<MyResource>("Permission:MyModule.MyEntity.Create")`

## Using Permissions
- Use `[Authorize("PermissionName")]` attribute on application services/controllers
- Use `[AllowAnonymous]` to allow unauthenticated access
- Use `AuthorizationService.CheckAsync("PermissionName")` for programmatic checks
- Use `AuthorizationService.IsGrantedAsync("PermissionName")` for conditional logic

## Permission Management
- Inject `IPermissionManager` to grant/revoke permissions programmatically
- Use `SetForUserAsync`, `SetForRoleAsync`, `SetForClientAsync` methods

## Multi-Tenancy
- Set `multiTenancySide` parameter: `MultiTenancySides.Host`, `Tenant`, or `Both`

## Feature/Global Feature Dependencies
- Use `.RequireFeatures("FeatureName")` to depend on features
- Use `.RequireGlobalFeatures("GlobalFeatureName")` to depend on global features
